<Base title="Affiliate Disclosure" description="How Bump Compass earns revenue, and what that means for you.">
  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="prose">
    <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>

    <p><em>Last updated: October 2026</em></p>

    <p>Bump Compass is free to use. We earn money when you buy something through certain links on this site. If you click one and make a purchase, we may earn a commission. <strong>You never pay more.</strong></p>

    <h2>How you'll know</h2>

    <p>Affiliate links carry a disclosure next to them:</p>

    <div class="affiliate-disclosure">
      <strong>Affiliate link:</strong> If you click this link and make a purchase, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you.
    </div>

    <h2>What it doesn't change</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>We recommend products because they are relevant to the guide you're reading — not because they pay a commission.</li>
      <li>We don't accept payment for positive reviews.</li>
      <li>Our clinical content is sourced to ACOG, NICHD, Mayo Clinic and NHS, and is unaffected by any commercial relationship.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where the money goes</h2>

    <p>Commission revenue pays for hosting, sourcing, and the time it takes to build and maintain these tools. We also display advertising.</p>

    <p>We participate in affiliate programs for pregnancy, baby and breastfeeding products. Current partners include Root'd, Earth Mama, The Spoiled Mama, Motherhood Maternity and Momcozy. This list changes as partnerships change.</p>

    <h2>FTC compliance</h2>

    <p>In line with the Federal Trade Commission's guidance on endorsements and testimonials (16 CFR Part 255), we disclose our material connections to the brands we mention.</p>

    <p>Questions? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
